"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.
Items, one per line:
{\"ref\":\"card:question\",\"text\":\"Can GPU docking make 54000 rotations affordable within CPU 3600-rotation workflow budgets, improving pose recovery across 4 unbound complexes?\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:hypothesis\",\"text\":\"GPU acceleration offsets denser rotational search, improving best50 DockQ within matched complete-workflow time and allocation cost.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_lever\",\"text\":\"GPU standard accelerates workflows by at least 1.05; dense completes CPU-standard budgets and improves best50 DockQ by 0.01 on 3 cases.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_not\",\"text\":\"GPU standard gains fall below 1.05, dense misses CPU-standard budgets, or best50 DockQ gains below 0.01 occur on 2 cases.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:test_summary\",\"text\":\"Build deadline-controlled workflow runner. Compare CPU 3600, GPU 3600 and GPU 54000 rotations across 4 fixed cases. Require agreement before 7 paired timing blocks with shared budgets. Report top-ranked and best among 50 predictions’ DockQ separately. Stop calibration at $9.87; stop entire plan at $100.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:closest_prior\",\"text\":\"MEGADOCK times 352 docking jobs up to 1260 GPUs; maximum rotations unspecified, leaving matched complete-workflow search budgets unresolved [prior].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"prior\",\"url\":\"https://www.bi.cs.titech.ac.jp/megadock/perform.html\",\"quote\":\"#GPUs  | 105  | 210  | 315  | 420  | 630  | 840  | 1,050  | 1,260\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:left_open\",\"text\":\"Whether 54000 rotations complete CPU-standard workflow budgets and improve best50 recovery without concealing rank1 regressions on these 4 unbound cases.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:anchor\",\"text\":\"CPU and GPU standard poses agree; native self-comparison and independent DockQ checks validate evaluation before dense scoring.\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"dockq\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11467047/\",\"quote\":\"The advantage of the DockQ score is that it is a continuous score in the [0, 1] range, from incorrect to high quality, which facilitates method comparisons since distributions, instead of classifications, of model quality scores can be compared.\"}],\"value\":\"Native self-score target 1, derived from DockQ formula with complete contacts and zero RMSDs [dockq].\"}
{\"ref\":\"card:limits\",\"text\":\"Four cases; exploratory history already exposed. Conditional runtime feasibility. No population inference, biological efficacy, guaranteed rank1 improvement or unseen-holdout claim.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"src:prior\",\"url\":\"https://www.bi.cs.titech.ac.jp/megadock/perform.html\",\"quote\":\"#GPUs  | 105  | 210  | 315  | 420  | 630  | 840  | 1,050  | 1,260\",\"supports\":\"Nearest opened official published performance result, not H100 complete workflow evidence; table covers 352 docking calculations on older hardware. Rotation count not established, so prior_max_level null.\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:dockq\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11467047/\",\"quote\":\"The advantage of the DockQ score is that it is a continuous score in the [0, 1] range, from incorrect to high quality, which facilitates method comparisons since distributions, instead of classifications, of model quality scores can be compared.\",\"supports\":\"Native-reference quality metric; equation supports self-comparison target 1. Engineering tolerances and improvement thresholds are DESIGN, not literature equivalence claims.\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:h100_price\",\"name\":\"H100 PCIe price per GPU\",\"value\":3.29,\"unit\":\"USD/GPU/hour\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"quote\":\"NVIDIA H100 PCIe | 80 GB | 26 | 225 GiB | 1 TiB SSD | $3.29\",\"page_setting\":\"Single H100 PCIe, 80 GB; 1x group supplied in price sheet and fetched matching row.\",\"url\":\"https://lambda.ai/pricing\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:rot_standard\",\"name\":\"Documented standard rotational sampling\",\"value\":3600,\"unit\":\"rotations\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"quote\":\"| `-D`                      |               | set the 6 deg. (54000 angles) of rotational sampling (default to none, 15 deg. (3600 angles) of rotational sampling)\",\"page_setting\":\"Pinned MEGADOCK standard sampling.\",\"url\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akiyamalab/MEGADOCK/9575280c875732553266e26adc607dd892b02616/doc/README.md\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:rot_dense\",\"name\":\"Documented dense rotational sampling\",\"value\":54000,\"unit\":\"rotations\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"quote\":\"| `-D`                      |               | set the 6 deg. (54000 angles) of rotational sampling (default to none, 15 deg. (3600 angles) of rotational sampling)\",\"page_setting\":\"Pinned MEGADOCK -D sampling.\",\"url\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akiyamalab/MEGADOCK/9575280c875732553266e26adc607dd892b02616/doc/README.md\"}

